# ResearchX rules

For research tasks, use the ResearchX skill (skills/researchx/):
1. Read skills/researchx/SKILL.md and follow its module router and quality gates.
2. Run the bundled stdlib scripts instead of guessing: verify_citations.py (citation verification),
   search_literature.py (structured retrieval), prisma_screen.py (screening + PRISMA counts),
   analyze_methods.py, generate_visuals.py. All accept --help.
3. Never emit a reference that verify_citations has not confirmed or that is not labelled [UNVERIFIED].
   Never state a number without a retrieved source.
4. Save outputs to files (analysis_*.md, topics_*.md, methods_*.md, manuscript_*.md, citation_audit_*.md).
5. If retrieval fails, say so and continue with labelled first-principles reasoning.
